# Better Auth & Multitenancy

Anti-hallucination file map. Every rule references an actual path in this repo.

## File map (source of truth)

| Concern | File | Export / API |
|---------|------|--------------|
| Auth config | `src/lib/auth.ts` | `auth` — Better Auth + `organization()` plugin, Resend emails, `databaseHooks.user.create.after` (personal org) |
| Auth API route | `src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts` | Single catch-all — do not create duplicate auth routes |
| Server session (org-aware) | `src/lib/org-server.ts` | `getServerSession()`, `requireSession()`, `requireOrganization()`, `getActiveOrganization()` |
| Server session (simple) | `src/lib/auth-server.ts` | `getServerSession()` only — prefer `org-server.ts` for protected features |
| Client auth | `src/lib/auth-client.ts` | `authClient` with `organizationClient()` plugin |
| Optimistic guard | `src/lib/auth-guard.ts` | `runAuthGuard()`, `PROTECTED_ROUTES`, `SENSITIVE_ROUTES`, locale stripping |
| Proxy (Next.js 16) | `src/proxy.ts` | next-intl + `runAuthGuard()` + rate limit on `/api/auth/*` |
| Tenant security | `src/lib/tenant-guard.ts` | `assertOrgMember()`, `scopeToActiveOrg()`, `requireOrgPermission()` |
| RBAC permissions | `src/lib/org-permissions.ts` | `can()`, `isOrgRole()`, `OrgPermission` type |
| Email | `src/lib/email.ts` | Resend; dev fallback logs to console |
| Auth hook (client) | `src/hooks/use-auth.tsx` | Client session wrapper |

## Rules

1. **NEVER** use Supabase, Firebase, Auth.js, or custom session JWT — Better Auth only
2. **NEVER** use deprecated `middleware.ts` — route protection is `src/proxy.ts` + `auth-guard.ts` (Next.js 16+)
3. **NEVER** use `getSessionCookie()` for authorization — optimistic redirect only; call `auth.api.getSession({ headers })` in RSC/actions
4. **ALWAYS** use `requireSession()` or `requireOrganization()` in server actions that need auth
5. **ALWAYS** call `requireOrgPermission()` before member/invitation/settings mutations
6. **NEVER** trust `organizationId` from client input — scope via `session.session.activeOrganizationId` + `assertOrgMember()`
7. Auth pages live at `src/app/[locale]/auth/**` — API stays at `/api/auth/*` (no locale prefix)
8. Redirects must include locale: use `withLocalePrefix()` or `@/i18n/navigation` `redirect({ href, locale })`
9. `SENSITIVE_ROUTES` (`/settings`, `/org`) require full server-side permission checks — proxy cookie check alone is insufficient
10. Personal org auto-created on signup via `databaseHooks` — do not duplicate this logic elsewhere
11. Google OAuth optional — gated by `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` + `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` in `src/env.ts`
12. Email verification required (`requireEmailVerification: true`) — account not fully active until verified

## Cross-reference

> For security policies (cookie flags, CSP, rate limits, secret handling), see `security.mdc`.
> For Prisma org models and queries, see `prisma.mdc`.
